cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  TEKWE3: A Design for Transactionally Consistent Hybrid Search in a
  Unified Tri-Modal Storage Engine
message: >-
  If you use or build on this design, please cite it using the metadata
  in this file.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: Hami
    name: Hami
repository-code: https://github.com/hami9/tekwe3
url: https://github.com/hami9/tekwe3
abstract: >-
  A complete engineering specification for a single-node storage engine in
  which key-value, full-text, and vector indexes live inside the same
  immutable segment, sharing one write-ahead log, one MVCC snapshot, and one
  compaction pipeline. Two observations make the composition possible: LSM
  compaction and Lucene segment merge are the same operation, and IVF vector
  partitions merge cheaply where HNSW graphs do not. A hybrid query -
  predicate filter, BM25, and approximate nearest neighbour - is served from a
  single log sequence number, making cross-index skew structurally zero rather
  than merely small. The specification includes the on-disk format, a
  fifteen-phase roadmap with falsifiable exit criteria, a
  deterministic-simulation-first correctness strategy, and a self-audit of its
  own gaps. It is a design; it has not been implemented or measured.
keywords:
  - storage engine
  - LSM tree
  - hybrid search
  - vector search
  - full-text search
  - MVCC
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - deterministic simulation testing
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: '2026-09-02'
version: '1.0'
